ough how the 1.10 multiplier fits into this formula.\n\nLooking at the test cases, I can see that the first-insurance surcharge and loyalty discount apply multiplicatively at the policy level, while item-specific surcharges like cursed and enchanted are additive per item. So the calculation stacks item surcharges first, then applies policy-level multipliers. For a second contract, the 1.10 first-insurance surcharge doesn't apply anymore, replaced by the 0.85 second-contract discount. The formula appears to be: calculate each item's base with its surcharges, sum those across items, then apply policy-level multipliers and the processing fee.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_018B26Jkp4ZhThER6yJSzB54","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"  it(\"applies 20% loyalty discount when yearsWithMHPCO >= 2 -- sword premium 93 (100*1.10*0.80+5)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }] });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });","oldText":"  it.todo(\"applies 20% loyalty discount when yearsWithMHPCO >= 2 -- sword premium 93 (100*1.10*0.80+5)\");"}],"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"bedrock/claude-opus-4-7@eu-west-1","usage":{"input":466,"output":1329,"cacheRead":30680,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":32475,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784853127574,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-c311d36f-5131-4c0b-9f85-aecca2490b99","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-7"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_bdrk_018B26Jkp4ZhThER6yJSzB54","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim-office.spec.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"    ...\n 41   it(\"quotes a cursed and highly enchanted sword (both surcharges) -- premium 203 (100*1.8*1.10+5)\", () => {\